    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Raju wanted to know whether 144 could be shared equally among 9 children.\n\"Add the digits,\" said Meena."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "divisible",
     "factor",
     "multiple"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A number is divisible by 2 if its last digit is even, by 5 if it ends in 0 or 5, by 10 if it ends in 0. It is divisible by 3 if the sum of its digits is, and by 9 if the digit sum is divisible by 9.\n144 has digit sum 9 so it is divisible by 9. 144 divided by 9 is 16.\nA factor divides a number exactly. Factors of 12 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 12."
    }
   },
